{
  "id": "typescript-14-ambient-declarations",
  "slug": "ambient-declarations",
  "title": "Ambient declarations and declare global",
  "moduleId": "typescript-14-modules-and-declarations",
  "order": 3,
  "hook": "**Ambient declarations** (`declare`) describe globals, assets, and env without emitting JS — `declare global`, wildcard `declare module \"*.css\"`, and `.d.ts` files.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "**declare** is type-only. **declare global** augments globals from a module file (needs `export {}`). **declare module \"*.css\"** types asset imports. `.d.ts` files never emit. **@types/*** from DefinitelyTyped for untyped JS libs."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "ambient",
              "longForm": "declare",
              "plainDefinition": "Types without JS output.",
              "example": "declare const API_URL: string"
            },
            {
              "term": "declare global",
              "longForm": "global augmentation",
              "plainDefinition": "Extend Window, process, etc.",
              "example": "declare global { interface Window { ... } }"
            },
            {
              "term": "wildcard module",
              "longForm": "declare module \"*.ext\"",
              "plainDefinition": "Type non-TS imports.",
              "example": "*.module.css"
            },
            {
              "term": "DefinitelyTyped",
              "longForm": "@types",
              "plainDefinition": "Community ambient types.",
              "example": "@types/node"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "process.env and window extensions need types. Vite import.meta.env augmentation. declare vs const — declare describes existing binding."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: declare vs const",
          "body": "declare describes existing runtime value — does not create it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Find global",
              "body": "window, process, script tag"
            },
            {
              "title": "Write .d.ts",
              "body": "type only"
            },
            {
              "title": "export {}",
              "body": "before declare global in .ts"
            },
            {
              "title": "Include in tsconfig",
              "body": "types or files"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Ambient vs value",
            "source": "flowchart TD\n  D[declare] --> TC[typecheck only]\n  C[const] --> EMIT[emits JS]"
